WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.649 --> 00:00:03.566
(melancholy music)

00:00:09.487 --> 00:00:12.170
- The produce industry
does not have the right

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.419
to dump nutritious product

00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:17.752
that can go to families who are in need.

00:00:24.249 --> 00:00:26.693
Borderlands Food Bank rescues between

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:30.109
30 to 40 million pounds
of produce annually,

00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:32.692
and we've been doing it for 21 years.

00:00:32.692 --> 00:00:35.359
(hopeful music)

00:00:44.603 --> 00:00:46.106
My name is Yolanda Soto,

00:00:46.106 --> 00:00:50.464
and I am the CEO-President
of Borderlands Food Bank.

00:00:50.464 --> 00:00:53.283
(upbeat music)

00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:57.565
We are an organization
that rescues fresh produce.

00:00:57.565 --> 00:01:01.552
We get it to families all
over the state of Arizona

00:01:01.552 --> 00:01:04.719
and 19 other states within the nation.

00:01:05.906 --> 00:01:09.197
We saw there was a tremendous
amount of fresh produce

00:01:09.197 --> 00:01:11.724
coming across at our port of entry here

00:01:11.724 --> 00:01:15.833
from Mexico, and a lot
of it could not be sold.

00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:18.191
It could be because it had some scarring,

00:01:18.191 --> 00:01:21.360
it could be because it
had some rain stain.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.603
And so they were actually
dumping it in the landfill.

00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:28.153
We saw that the product was extremely good

00:01:28.153 --> 00:01:29.836
for human consumption,

00:01:29.836 --> 00:01:32.547
so we began educating
the produce industry.

00:01:32.547 --> 00:01:35.448
(cheerful music)

00:01:35.448 --> 00:01:38.602
We've gone to each individual distributor.

00:01:38.602 --> 00:01:40.927
We've offered them our services and said,

00:01:40.927 --> 00:01:42.318
"Do not dump.

00:01:42.318 --> 00:01:45.511
"Allow us to rescue it
and get it to families

00:01:45.511 --> 00:01:49.085
"so that they can eat nutritiously."

00:01:49.085 --> 00:01:50.790
The driver comes back to the warehouse,

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.578
he's got a trailer-load of product,

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:55.078
and he begins to get unloaded.

00:01:56.341 --> 00:01:58.638
We take up the produce to the sites,

00:01:58.638 --> 00:02:00.993
and we set it up like a farmer's market,

00:02:00.993 --> 00:02:04.493
all done by volunteers from the host site.

00:02:05.384 --> 00:02:07.681
For a $10 contribution,

00:02:07.681 --> 00:02:11.541
the supporter can select
60 pounds of produce.

00:02:11.541 --> 00:02:14.212
Pretty good, $0.17 a pound.

00:02:14.212 --> 00:02:17.062
(cheerful music)

00:02:17.062 --> 00:02:19.168
It's important to us to get it to

00:02:19.168 --> 00:02:22.976
as many families as
possible before it perishes,

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.419
because I think that people

00:02:24.419 --> 00:02:26.295
have the right to eat nutritiously,

00:02:26.295 --> 00:02:28.463
it's the most basic of needs.

00:02:28.463 --> 00:02:30.456
Thank you, have a great day.

00:02:30.456 --> 00:02:32.623
We have the responsibility

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.048
to stop waste,

00:02:36.048 --> 00:02:37.787
and we have the responsibility

00:02:37.787 --> 00:02:41.037
to help the people in our own backyard.

